WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.168
-It's becoming clear

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.270
that President Trump
has no way out

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.573
of the government shutdown
he's boxed himself into.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.941
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.941 --> 00:00:13.413 line:0%
[ Suspenseful theme plays ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:16.182
The shutdown is having real
effects for millions of people

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.817
and that includes
law enforcement officials

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.219
going without pay.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.786
Yesterday, in his
confirmation hearing,

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:23.322
Trump's pick for attorney
general, William Barr,

00:00:23.322 --> 00:00:25.492
was asked about the effect
on law enforcement

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.494
and said the shutdown was
the fault of both sides.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:30.529
- People would like to see
the shutdown ended

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:33.365
and that's why people wanna see
some kind of compromise

00:00:33.365 --> 00:00:36.402
and, you know, you call it
the Trump shutdown,

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:38.337
but, I mean,
it takes two to tango.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.540
-Okay, but this is not a tango.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.475
Trump is the only one dancing.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:44.209
[ Laughter ]
And, judging from how

00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:46.779
he moves his hands, he's doing
some off-brand version

00:00:46.779 --> 00:00:48.782
of the Macarena.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.617
I mean, look at 'im. He looks
like a grandpa at a wedding.

00:00:51.617 --> 00:00:54.019
[ Laughter ]
♪ Hey, macaroni ♪

00:00:54.019 --> 00:00:55.688
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.089
It's not both sides.

00:00:57.089 --> 00:00:59.025
We all remember the meeting
in the Oval Office

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.760
where Trump literally said
he was proud

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:02.094
to shut down the government
and, yet,

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:04.330
despite the fact
that he is on camera,

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.932
saying the shutdown
would be his fault,

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.201
Trump actually thinks he's
winning the argument.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:10.069
CNN reported yesterday
that Trump has been

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:12.671
telling aides and allies
that he believes

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:14.807
he is winning the battle
for public support.

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:16.509
Well, of course
he believes that.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.078
He watches more Fox News
than all the residents

00:01:19.078 --> 00:01:21.213
of a Texas senior center,
combined.

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:22.381
[ Laughter and light clapping ]

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:24.450
Trump always thinks he
can win any fight.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.386
He can be in the Octagon
with Conor McGregor,

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.721
takin' a kick to the face,
and he'd say, "Did you see?

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:30.789
I just head-butted his foot
with my face."

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:32.358
[ Laughter and light clapping ]

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.026
Trump also thinks
his Oval Office speech

00:01:34.026 --> 00:01:35.161
on the wall last week

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.729
really moved public opinion
to his side.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.697
Now, you might be asking
yourself, "Wait,

00:01:38.697 --> 00:01:40.733
Trump gave a speech from the
Oval Office last week?"

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:43.903
And that's because everyone
has already forgotten about it.

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.971
[ Laughter ]
That speech was only a week ago

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:49.342
and it's already been eclipsed
by several insane news stories,

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:51.510
from Trump's trip
to the southern border

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.347
to the fact that the FBI thought
he was a Russian asset,

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.782
to the fact that
the White House

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:59.451
is serving so much fast food,
they've added a drive-thru.

00:01:59.451 --> 00:02:01.955
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.056
What's next, is he gonna --

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:05.290
[ Applause ]

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.595
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.664
Is he gonna try to achieve
peace in the Middle East

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.232
with a summit
at Chuck E. Cheese?

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:17.536
[as Trump] No quarters for
anyone 'til you sort this out.

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:19.706
[ Laughter ]
So, yes, Trump really did

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.774
give a primetime address
on the wall last week

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:24.410
and he thinks it helped sway
public opinion to his side,

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:27.212
but the actually polling
says something very different.

00:02:27.212 --> 00:02:29.449
-Within the last half hour,
Quinnipiac has come out

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:32.485
with a new poll, asking,
"Did the president's speech

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.852
last week from the Oval Office

00:02:33.852 --> 00:02:34.921
[ Laughter ]
change your mind

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:37.891
about the wall?"
Only 2% said yes.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.592
-2%?!

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.261
Maybe the speech
only polled at 2%

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:45.732
because Trump's eye
was only 2% open.

00:02:45.732 --> 00:02:47.400
That's why he thinks
he can win any fight.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.336
He's Popeye, except, with bacon,
instead of spinach.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:53.072
[ Laughter ]
Trump's argument is not working

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:54.740
'cause it's detached
from reality.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.943
It's also very hard to follow.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:59.879
For example, Trump has recently
found a new favorite line

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.481
that he keeps repeating at all
of his public appearances:

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:07.086
"Walls work
because cars have wheels."

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.454
-They say a wall is medieval.

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:10.122
Well, so is a wheel.

00:03:10.122 --> 00:03:12.458
A wheel is older than a wall.

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:13.659
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.659 --> 00:03:15.761
And I looked and every
single car out there,

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.596
even the really expenses ones,

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.999
[ Laughter ]
that the Secret Service uses --

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:22.201
and believe me,
they are expensive.

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:23.703
I said,
"Do they all have wheels?"

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.905
"Yes."
Oh, I thought it was medieval.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.574
The wheel is older than
the wall, you know that?

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:31.510
And, uh, there are
some things that work.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:34.614
You know what?
A wheel works and a wall works.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.549
They say it's medieval.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.984
Well, so is the wheel, medieval.

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:41.454
I looked at all the vans and all
of the serious equipment

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.990
that they surrounded me with
yesterday.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.692
-Mm.
-The Secret Service, the police,

00:03:46.692 --> 00:03:49.128
the Border Patrol, ICE.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.929
Every one of those
had the wheel.

00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:53.699
Well, they say wheels
are medieval, too.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.501
But some things don't change.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.237
Wheels and walls.

00:03:58.237 --> 00:03:59.339
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.339 --> 00:04:01.440
-Hey, um,

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.542
I'm worried about Grandpa.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.610
[ Laughter ]

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.345
Yeah, no. It's, uh --

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:07.980
[ Applause and cheering ]
Yeah.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.482
[ Whistling ]

00:04:09.482 --> 00:04:12.418
[ Applause ]

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.219
No, it's a wheel wall.
Yeah, it's a wheel wall.

00:04:14.219 --> 00:04:16.755
[ Laughter ]
I gotta go.

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:18.725
He just keeps saying the same
things over and over.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.493
In other words,
he's hitting a wall

00:04:20.493 --> 00:04:22.328
and it's his brain is going
around like a wheel.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:23.729
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.729 --> 00:04:25.665
But I guess, now, we know what
Trump's been doing all day

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.200
in the Oval Office
during the shutdown:

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.801
Just starin' out the window,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.936
countin' all the wheels
on the car.

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.771
[ Laughter ]
One, two, three, four.

00:04:32.771 --> 00:04:33.840
One, two,
three, four.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.842
Oh, no, a bus!
This isn't gonna be easy.

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:37.643
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.643 --> 00:04:40.446
Now, as dumb as Trump's argument
is, he was actually going

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.548
to get another chance
to make it later this month,

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:43.916
to yet another
primetime audience,

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:45.684
for his annual
State of the Union address.

00:04:45.684 --> 00:04:48.287
But presidents technically
have to be invited

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:50.623
to give the State of the Union
by the speaker of the House

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.358
and, today,
because of the shutdown,

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:55.127
Speaker Nancy Pelosi
asked Trump to reschedule

00:04:55.127 --> 00:04:58.097
his State of the Union address
or deliver it in writing.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.598
[ Laughter ]
That's such a great burn

00:04:59.598 --> 00:05:01.567
because, you know,
when Trump heard reschedule,

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:02.901
he thought, [as Trump] "Yes!"

00:05:02.901 --> 00:05:04.270
But when he heard deliver it
in writing, he thought,

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.706
[as Trump] "No-o-o-o-o!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:09.241
I would love to see Trump write
down his State of the Union.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:11.710
I can imagine what
that would look like.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.713
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.614
It's fun!

00:05:15.614 --> 00:05:16.783
It's fun.

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:20.553
[ Cheering, whistling,
and applause ]

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:23.156
Fun, picturing Trump sittin'
down at a typewriter,

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:26.292
punchin' the keys one at a time
with his sweaty hand paws.

00:05:26.292 --> 00:05:27.860
[ Laughter ]
[as Trump] Is wall spelled

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.295
with one L or four?

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.030
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.598
I'll just use all the L's.

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:35.067
[ Laughter ]
What we're witnessing right now

00:05:35.067 --> 00:05:37.569
are the desperate gasps
of the Trump agenda.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:39.538
The wall was
the signature promise

00:05:39.538 --> 00:05:41.240
of his campaign and presidency.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.275
He's been talkin' about it
for three and a half years,

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:45.210
but, now, it's slipping away,

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.545
with Democrats
in control of the House,

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:49.048
and, in his desperation
to save face and get a deal,

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.550
Trump is throwing everything
he said about the wall

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:52.784
out the window.

00:05:52.784 --> 00:05:54.854
For example, he said
Democrats didn't even have

00:05:54.854 --> 00:05:58.691
to call it a wall and offered
one very strange suggestion.

00:05:58.691 --> 00:06:01.026
-This is where I asked
the Democrats to come back

00:06:01.026 --> 00:06:06.565
to Washington and to vote
for money for the wall,

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:10.002
the barrier, whatever you
wanna call it's okay with me.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.203
They can name it whatever.

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:14.006
They can name it Peaches.

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.441
[ Laughter ]
I don't care what they name it.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:19.045
-They should call his bluff
and name it Donald Trump's BO.

00:06:19.045 --> 00:06:20.379
[ Laughter ]

00:06:20.379 --> 00:06:22.048
Then, his supporters
would have to say,

00:06:22.048 --> 00:06:24.317
"Donald Trump's BO
has been very effective

00:06:24.317 --> 00:06:26.085
in keeping immigrants
out of the country."

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:27.286
[ Laughter ]

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:28.654
And that isn't even
the weirdest suggestion

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.522
for what the wall should be
called because, last week,

00:06:30.522 --> 00:06:33.459
Louisiana Republican
Senator John Kennedy said,

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:34.727
"You can call it a barrier.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:36.028
You can call it a wall.

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.363
You can call it a wang doodle,

00:06:37.363 --> 00:06:38.798
[ Laughter ]
for all I care.

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:42.568
Wang doodle and peaches don't
sound like names for a wall.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:45.571
They sound like a euphemism
for a guy's junk.

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:47.506
[ Laughter ]
Did you hear about Rudy?

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.408
He accidentally sat
on his wang doodle

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:50.509
and banged it into his peaches

00:06:50.509 --> 00:06:52.077
and that explains
why he looks like that.

00:06:52.077 --> 00:06:54.379
[ Applause and cheering ]

00:06:54.379 --> 00:06:55.715
So, now --

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:58.083
[ Applause ]

00:06:58.083 --> 00:07:00.519
Now, Trump is throwing out all
of his campaign promises

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:02.588
about the wall and saying
Democrats can call it

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:04.590
whatever they want,
but one thing he guaranteed,

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.593
the one thing that was crucial
to the whole idea

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.662
was that it would be
impossible to get through.

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:13.065
-So we're gonna build a wall
and it's gonna be impenetrable.

00:07:13.065 --> 00:07:18.371
We will begin working
on an impenetrable, physical,

00:07:18.371 --> 00:07:23.909
tall, powerful, beautiful,
southern border wall.

00:07:23.909 --> 00:07:25.444
-Physical, powerful,
and beautiful.

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:26.645
Was he building a wall

00:07:26.645 --> 00:07:28.748
or setting up a Tinder
profile for it?

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.048
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.048 --> 00:07:31.783
[as Trump] Physical, tall,
powerful, beautiful,

00:07:31.783 --> 00:07:33.252
works hard, plays harder.

00:07:33.252 --> 00:07:35.855
[ Laughter ]
And, as dumb as the wall is,

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:38.090
literally the only point
to building one

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:41.427
is to make it impenetrable
and Trump repeatedly promised

00:07:41.427 --> 00:07:43.128
he could do it
because that's what he does.

00:07:43.128 --> 00:07:44.564
He's a builder!

00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:49.869
-Look, as a builder, nobody
in the history of this country

00:07:49.869 --> 00:07:52.638
has ever known so much about
infrastructure as Donald Trump.

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.240
I build infrastructure.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.075
Do I know how to build a wall?

00:07:56.075 --> 00:07:57.777
Our nation's in such trouble.

00:07:57.777 --> 00:08:00.313
That's why being a builder,
and a great builder,

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:03.249
and a very successful builder,
I think, will greatly help.

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:05.884
Donald Trump, another
great builder in New York,

00:08:05.884 --> 00:08:07.419
now a politician.

00:08:07.419 --> 00:08:09.889
I can't stand this.
A politician!

00:08:09.889 --> 00:08:11.423
I don't wanna be called
a politician.

00:08:11.423 --> 00:08:12.758
-Oh, don't worry.

00:08:12.758 --> 00:08:14.927
No one --
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:14.927 --> 00:08:17.562
No one thinks
you're a politician.

00:08:17.562 --> 00:08:19.165
We think of you as a politician

00:08:19.165 --> 00:08:21.534
the way we think of Shaq
as a movie star.

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:23.435
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.435 --> 00:08:25.838
So, the only point
in building a wall is

00:08:25.838 --> 00:08:27.940
to make it impenetrable
and, yet, last week,

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.176
it was reported that testing
of a prototype proved

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:31.577
it could be cut through
with a saw.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.212
And they even got a photo
of the wall

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.680
after it had been sawed open.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.016
Last week, Trump was asked
about that report

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:38.317
and the guy
who repeatedly promised

00:08:38.317 --> 00:08:40.085
an impenetrable wall
said this --

00:08:40.085 --> 00:08:41.820
-What good is a steel wall
if they can saw through it?

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.457
-Well, that's a wall that
was designed

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:46.926
by previous administrations.

00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:51.830
There's nothing that can't be
penetrated, but you fix it.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:54.366
But it's a very difficult
thing to do.

00:08:54.366 --> 00:08:56.502
But that's a wall,
and they have other walls.

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.804
We have many
walls under consideration.

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:00.873
[ Laughter ]
-I love how you can tell

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:03.308
when Trump is lying,
because he circles

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:06.145
through every explanation
he can think of in five seconds.

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.613
[as Trump]
It was Obama's fault.

00:09:07.613 --> 00:09:10.082
Nothing is impenetrable.
We have other walls.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:12.084
[ Laughter ]
Next, he's gonna say,

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.485
[as Trump] They can't saw
through the new one

00:09:13.485 --> 00:09:15.554
because we made it out of saws.

00:09:15.554 --> 00:09:17.256
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:19.624
All right, but so what?
Maybe they can just find a new,

00:09:19.624 --> 00:09:22.294
stronger material and make sure
the wall's impenetrable.

00:09:22.294 --> 00:09:23.462
Problem solved, right?

00:09:23.462 --> 00:09:25.097
I mean, it's not like
there's some other,

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:27.500
superobvious way
to get around a wall.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.635
-During a roundtable discussion
with law enforcement officials,

00:09:29.635 --> 00:09:32.070
Mr. Trump was told
some border crossers

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:33.338
had been digging tunnels

00:09:33.338 --> 00:09:37.009
under areas where walls
are already in place.

00:09:37.009 --> 00:09:40.312
-Here, this is just a couple
miles from here,

00:09:40.312 --> 00:09:41.613
from where we're standing.

00:09:41.613 --> 00:09:43.649
This is a tunnel.

00:09:43.649 --> 00:09:46.885
This is the second tunnel that,
recently, we have located.

00:09:46.885 --> 00:09:49.788
This is an area
that we actually have wall.

00:09:49.788 --> 00:09:51.957
- That's right.
They already had a wall there

00:09:51.957 --> 00:09:54.259
and someone just
tunneled under it.

00:09:54.259 --> 00:09:56.762
[ Laughter ]
Trump's wall is so stupid that,

00:09:56.762 --> 00:09:58.630
not only can it be beaten
by a saw;

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:00.299
it can be beaten by Bugs Bunny.

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:01.833
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.833 --> 00:10:03.936
In fact, if you listen
to Trump explain

00:10:03.936 --> 00:10:06.138
how he thinks migrants sneak
across the southern border,

00:10:06.138 --> 00:10:09.308
he might actually be thinking
about Bugs Bunny.

00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:13.279
-They get off the road and they
drive out into the desert

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:15.180
and they come on.
They make a left turn.

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:16.682
Usually, it's a left,
not a right.

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:20.518
-I knew I shoulda taken
that left toin at Albuquerque.

00:10:20.518 --> 00:10:21.954
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:21.954 --> 00:10:25.524
-Every day, we find out more
about how useless the wall is

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:27.993
and that's why public opinion
is against it.

00:10:27.993 --> 00:10:30.295
Every time Trump sees
a new poll about the shutdown,

00:10:30.295 --> 00:10:31.563
it's like a kick,

00:10:31.563 --> 00:10:33.832
in the wang doodle and...
-Peaches.

00:10:33.832 --> 00:10:35.233
[ Laughter ]
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:10:35.233 --> 00:10:39.105
♪♪
[ Cheering and applause ]

